+{% set source = config.LEAN_SOURCE %}
+{% block body %}<h2>About this book</h2>
+<p>This is a reading of Levent Alpöge's Lean proof of the Riemann Hypothesis and of the Generalized Riemann Hypothesis for Dirichlet $L$-functions; a working draft, not Alpöge's own exposition. The statements, proofs and notes were written from the Lean, and their mistakes are not Alpöge's.</p>
+<h3>Sources</h3>
+<p>Alpöge announced the proof in <a href="{{ source.announcement.url }}">{{ source.announcement.url }}</a> on {{ source.announcement.date }}. The Lean proof is published as an archive in {{ source.archive.parts | length }} parts, <a href="{{ source.archive.parts[0].url }}">{{ source.archive.parts[0].url.rsplit('/', 1)[1] }}</a> to <a href="{{ source.archive.parts[-1].url }}">{{ source.archive.parts[-1].url.rsplit('/', 1)[1] }}</a> at <a href="{{ source.archive.parts[0].url.rsplit('/', 1)[0] }}/">{{ source.archive.parts[0].url.rsplit('/', 1)[0] }}</a>. The joined archive has SHA-256</p>
+<p><code class="archive-digest">{{ source.archive.sha256 }}</code></p>
+<p>Its toolchain is <code>{{ source.toolchain }}</code>, with Mathlib at <code>{{ source.mathlib.rev }}</code>. The book cites this archive only. Each statement links to the declarations of the archive it corresponds to, on this site's copy of the Lean sources, and its correspondence note says where the Lean and the text differ. The links are checked against the archive when the book is built; the prose is not checked against the Lean by any machine.</p>
+<h3>Tags</h3>
+<p>Each chapter, section and statement has a permanent four-character tag, beginning with <code>Z</code>. A tag is never reassigned or reused, so links to tags survive renumbering. These are not Stacks Project tags.</p>
+<h3>Software</h3>
+<p>This edition is built with <a href="https://gerby-project.github.io/">Gerby</a>, the open-source system developed by Pieter Belmans and Raymond Cheng: its <a href="https://github.com/gerby-project/plastex/tree/a75473f890db3d21e3bf76430c5c1ffc0661a69a">plasTeX Gerby renderer</a> and <a href="https://github.com/gerby-project/gerby-website/tree/01b11bbbbd1a910bc997eb3d53bd1cd8c8de8652">Gerby website application</a>, with the local patches of Resolution's Hironaka book and of this book.</p>
+<p>Typography and colors follow <a href="https://resolution.org/">Resolution</a>. The reading layout is inspired by LessWrong. Its progress-line interpolation and contents scaling are adapted from <a href="https://github.com/ForumMagnum/ForumMagnum/tree/a1665ead02e2c00647c098797979c4c994980673/packages/lesswrong/components/posts/TableOfContents">ForumMagnum</a>, with the <a href="/static/third-party/forum-magnum/LICENSE">GPL version 3 license</a>, original sources, and modification notes distributed with this edition.</p>
